      "created_at": "2014-11-11T04:32:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>What happens when you play one of these cards, and there are only two cards remaining in the relevant deck?</p><p>A) Nothing happens, because \"Reveal three cards\" can't resolve.&nbsp; No cards are revealed or moved.</p><p>B) The card does as much as it can.&nbsp; Two cards are revealed.&nbsp; The player puts one on the top of the deck, as ordered, then puts one on the bottom.&nbsp; There is no third card to also put on the bottom, but that's OK.</p><p>C) Something else...</p><p>It's a rare edge case for this to be possible, and even rarer for it to *matter* what order those last two cards are in -- but I wanna know!</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:51.056Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
